          "unit": "C",
          "value": 20
        },
        "notes": "Traditional decoction mash, eg for continental lagers.  Each later step is reached by drawing off part of the mash (mostly grain), boiling it and returning it to the main mash.\n\nWater amounts and temperatures depend on the recipe, so are not set here.  To use this profile, select it on a recipe's Mash tab and click \"Calculate Water…\".  (As the profile is locked, you will be asked whether to make a copy for the recipe, which you can then change as you wish.)",
